## Dev Notes

### No migration required

`DataPanel.svelte` and `GET /api/data/tasks` use no new DB tables. The Tableau worksheet is read client-side via the Extensions API; Google Docs is an external call via the existing `GoogleDocsIntegration` stub. No new Alembic version needed.

### Workflow config backwards compatibility

`data_panel` is optional in `WorkflowConfigSchema`. Existing configs that lack this field will still validate (`model_validate` ignores unknown fields by default in Pydantic v2 — note: this also means extra fields pass silently). Configs already stored in DB are re-parsed by `get_tool_definitions()` and `validate_schema()` — adding an optional field does not break those calls.

### Tableau worksheet API — dev/test fallback

`getWorksheetData()` returns `[]` immediately when no Tableau runtime is present. This means `DataPanel.svelte` in dev will show "No data available" in the worksheet section — expected. Tests do not need to mock the Tableau runtime.

### Google Docs stub — current behaviour

`GoogleDocsIntegration.execute()` always raises `IntegrationError("google_docs", "Google Docs not configured")`. The `GET /api/data/tasks` endpoint catches this and returns 503. The DataPanel frontend catches 503 (as `ApiError`) and shows the error in the tasks section while the worksheet section remains unaffected.

### `Promise.allSettled` is mandatory

Must use `Promise.allSettled` (not `Promise.all`) for the two independent data fetches in `onMount`. `Promise.all` rejects on first failure — this would break the NFR9 isolation guarantee.

### `_google_docs` as module-level singleton

Follows the pattern of `_INTEGRATION_MAP` in `app/api/integrations.py`. Module-level singleton is acceptable in v1 (single-process async). Avoid instantiating `GoogleDocsIntegration()` inside the request handler.

### Generic rendering — no field name coupling

The worksheet table renders `Object.keys(row[0])` as column headers. If the Tableau data source adds or renames a field, the panel still renders correctly. No conditional logic like `if col === "open_days"` anywhere in `DataPanel.svelte`.

